named.thread:
thread (core): This thread: status, last turn, context, cost, tokens, changes, plan.
  thread.turns: number
  thread.id thread.title thread.agent thread.model thread.effort thread.access thread.computer thread.project thread.folder thread.waitingOn: string
  thread.status: starting|working|needs-you|failed|done|resting
  thread.lastTurn: { status, durationMs, waitedMs, startedAt, endedAt, model }
  thread.cost: { usd }
  thread.tokens: { input, output, cached, cacheWrite, reasoning }
  thread.context: { used, window, free, percent }
  thread.changes: { files: { path, kind, additions, deletions }[], from, to, moved: any[], shared }
  thread.plan: { steps: { text, state: pending|working|done }[], text }
  thread.subagents: { id, title, state, startedAt, endedAt }[]
  thread.messages: { recent: { who, at, text }[], last }
update: push; scope: the slate's own thread; cost: none beyond today
note thread.context: the latest turn that reports it; null on an agent that does not
note thread.changes.files: the latest session.changes
example: {percent(thread.context.used / thread.context.window)}
The pieces and rules: slate_catalog with no name.

named.tree:
tree (working): The thread's root and every thread under it.
  tree.root: { id, title, status, agent, computer }
  tree.parent: { id, title, status, agent, computer }
  tree.children: { id, title, status, agent, computer, costUsd, startedAt, endedAt }[]
  tree.all: { id, title, status, agent, computer, depth }[]
  tree.counts: { working, needsYou, done, failed, resting }
update: push; scope: the thread's tree; cost: none beyond today
example: {tree.counts.working}
The pieces and rules: slate_catalog with no name.

named.usage:
usage (core): The plan windows of the account the thread runs on.
  usage.readAt: time
  usage.note: string
  usage.account: { key, label, agent, plan, address, computers: string[] }
  usage.windows: { kind: session|week|week_opus|week_sonnet|month|overage, usedPercent, resetsAt }[]
  usage.session: { percent, resetsAt }
  usage.week: { percent, resetsAt }
  usage.status: ok|warning|reached
  usage.burn: { tokensPerMinute, threads }
  usage.credits: { count, nextExpiresAt }
update: push; scope: the account the thread runs on; cost: one event per turn end
note usage.windows: Claude Code and Codex report them; a keyed sign-in has none and usage.note says why
example: {pct(usage.week.percent)}
The pieces and rules: slate_catalog with no name.

named.machine:
machine (working): The thread's computer: load, memory, disk and their last minute.
  machine.at: time
  machine.cpu machine.load1: number
  machine.name: string
  machine.mem: { used, total }
  machine.disk: { used, total }
  machine.history: { cpu: { x, y }[], load1: { x, y }[], mem: { x, y }[] }
update: subscription; scope: the thread's computer; cost: one sample a second while bound
example: {bytes(machine.mem.used)}
The pieces and rules: slate_catalog with no name.

named.mcp:
mcp (working): The thread's agent's MCP servers: consent state, tools, resources.
  mcp.<server>: { state: unasked|asked|allowed|refused|down, tools: { name, title, description, inputSchema: any, annotations: any, ui }[], resources: { uri, name, mimeType, description }[] }
update: push; scope: servers configured for the thread's agent; cost: a listing on connect
example: {mcp.linear.state}
